
Limited commands available
--------------------------

[Please run "/tmp/opencode/qit-212-1.3.2.phar connect" to connect to QIT.]

Quality Insights Toolkit CLI 1.3.2

Usage:
  command [options] [arguments]

Options:
  -h, --help            Display help for the given command. When no command is given display help for the list command
  -q, --quiet           Do not output any message
  -V, --version         Display this application version
      --ansi|--no-ansi  Force (or disable --no-ansi) ANSI output
  -n, --no-interaction  Do not ask any interactive question
  -v|vv|vvv, --verbose  Increase the verbosity of messages: 1 for normal output, 2 for more verbose output and 3 for debug

Available commands:
  connect             Connect to manage your extensions and test runs.
  help                Display help for a command
 blueprint
  blueprint:export    Exports a qit.json environment as a WordPress Playground Blueprint.
  blueprint:import    Converts a WordPress Playground Blueprint into a qit.json environment block.
 claude-tip
  claude-tip:dismiss  Permanently dismiss the Claude Code plugin recommendation
 env
  env:down            [env:stop] Stops a local test environment.
  env:enter           Enter the PHP container of a running test environment.
  env:exec            Execute a command inside the PHP container of a running test environment.
  env:list            List running environments.
  env:reset           Restore the post-setup database snapshot and flush the WordPress object cache
  env:source          Configure your shell to run tests against a QIT environment
  env:up              [env:start] Creates a temporary local test environment that is completely ephemeral
 partner
  partner:add         Configure a new WCCOM Marketplace Partner that the QIT CLI can connect to.
 qit
  qit:dir             Prints the QIT config directory path.
 tunnel
  tunnel:set-default  Set the default tunneling method for QIT CLI.
  tunnel:setup        Configure tunneling methods for QIT CLI.
 woo
  woo:validate-zip    Validate a local ZIP file's content.
